{{also|remédiation}}
==English==

===Etymology===
1818, noun of action from stem of Latin remediare, from remedium "a cure, remedy". In educational jargon by 1966; of pollution, by 1986. The modern uses might be new coinages from remediate (v.).

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# The process of [[remedy]]ing a situation.
#: ''The site required extensive environmental '''remediation''' before it could be used for other purposes.''

